triage: fix_game: Dealing works: each seat holds 5 cards after one trick, the deck is empty, and the turned and hidden cards are set. But the bid step never offers the options 0 to 6. In every failing scenario the seats were never offered 0 (or 6), and the stored bid stayed at 0 when the test chose 3 and 6, so the bid is not implemented as the rules and interface require.
step C: building the game file
step D: evaluating
triage: fix_game: Cards played to a trick are put back into the table deck (the deck holds 10D, QD and JD after trick 1), and the deck is never rebuilt at the start of a new hand. So when hand 2 is dealt, the game draws from a nearly empty list and crashes with an index out of range. The rules deal all 20 cards each hand, and trick cards simply leave play.
